course: dictionary
lesson: 11838
title: Animal sounds and whining words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can name a sound. A bleat is the shaky «baa» that a sheep, lamb or goat makes. «The lamb gave a small bleat when it lost its mum in the field.» The words lamb, field and mum tell you the bleat is an animal sound on a farm.
explain: Bleat can also be a doing word, a verb. «The goats bleated loudly at the gate.» Here bleated means the goats made that baa sound. Check by swapping in «made a baa sound». If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Sometimes people use bleat in a different way, and this is informal. «Stop bleating about your homework, Sam!» Sam is not making an animal sound. Bleating here means complaining in a weak, whining way, like a child who keeps moaning.
fact: A bleat is the shaky «baa» sound made by a sheep, lamb or goat.
fact: To bleat means to make that sound: «The lamb bleated for its mum.»
fact: Bleat can be a noun or a verb, and its forms are bleat, bleats, bleated and bleating.
fact: Informal use: «bleat on about» means to keep complaining in a weak, whining way.
fact: Like a dog barks and a cow moos, a sheep bleats.
exercise: What sound does a sheep make? | *A shaky baa, called a bleat | Moo | Neigh | Bark
exercise: «The goats bleated at the gate.» What does bleated mean here? | Ran away fast | *Made a shaky baa sound | Ate all the grass | Jumped over the gate
exercise: «Stop bleating about your homework.» What does bleating mean here? | Singing a happy song | Running around the room | Counting to ten | *Complaining in a weak, whining way
test: «The farmer heard a bleat from the hill.» What made the bleat? | Cow | Dog | *Sheep | Horse
test: «Lara keeps bleating on about her sore finger.» What is Lara doing? | Measuring her finger | Calling her dog | *Complaining in a whining way | Playing the piano
exam: In «The bleat of the lamb echoed across the field», what kind of word is bleat? | Adjective | *Noun | Verb | Adverb
